{"id":28734,"slug":"a-taste-of-honey","title":"A Taste of Honey","year":1961,"country":"United Kingdom","duration":100,"spine":829,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/28734-a-taste-of-honey","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/7bfaa9a3f92e2fc8b4cc5f8b3a72fcd4/sAyvt3qLGVUlBaHDDLG1vMF24HKrUk_large.jpg","description":"The revolutionary British New Wave films of the early 1960s were celebrated for their uncompromising depictions of working-class lives and relations between the sexes. Directed by Tony Richardson, a leading light of that movement, and based on one of the most controversial plays of its time, A Taste of Honey features Rita Tushingham in her star-making debut role as a disaffected teenager finding her way amid the economic desperation of industrial Manchester, and despite her absent, self-absorbed mother. With its unapologetic identification with social outcasts and its sensitive, modern approach to matters of sexuality and race, Richardson’s classic is a still startling benchmark work of realism.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Tony Richardson","slug":"tony-richardson"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Rita Tushingham","role":"Jo","slug":"rita-tushingham"},{"actor":"Dora Bryan","role":"Helen","slug":"dora-bryan"},{"actor":"Paul Danquah","role":"Jimmy","slug":"paul-danquah"},{"actor":"Murray Melvin","role":"Geoffrey","slug":"murray-melvin"},{"actor":"Robert Stephens","role":"Peter","slug":"robert-stephens"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Tony Richardson","slug":"tony-richardson"},{"role":"Produced by","person":"Tony Richardson","slug":"tony-richardson"},{"role":"Screenplay by","person":"Shelagh Delaney","slug":null},{"role":"Screenplay by","person":"Tony Richardson","slug":"tony-richardson"},{"role":"Adapted from the play by","person":"Shelagh Delaney","slug":null},{"role":"Music by","person":"John Addison","slug":null},{"role":"Cinematography by","person":"Walter Lassally","slug":null},{"role":"Film editing by","person